#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:10
msgctxt "Small badge beside the product name; labels this page as an interactive demo/sandbox, not a children's playground"
msgid "playground"
msgstr "démo"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:21
msgctxt "Tooltip on a status dot. 'isReady()' is an API name — keep it verbatim. 'gate UI on this' = show the UI only once it is ready; 'flash-of-untranslated-content' is the technical term for untranslated text briefly showing (FOUC)"
msgid "isReady() — gate UI on this to avoid flash-of-untranslated-content"
msgstr "isReady() — conditionner l'affichage de l'interface utilisateur à cet état pour éviter le flash de contenu non traduit"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:29
msgid "ready"
msgstr "prêt"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:29
msgid "loading…"
msgstr "chargement…"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:57
msgctxt "Heading above the sidebar table-of-contents navigation links"
msgid "On this page"
msgstr "Sur cette page"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:84
msgctxt "Hero tagline (marketing register). 'Angular' is the framework name and 'i18n' the abbreviation for internationalization — keep both. 'signal-first' means built around Angular Signals; render the technical sense, not 'first signal'"
msgid "Angular i18n, the signal-first way"
msgstr "i18n Angular, l'approche signal-first"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:91
msgctxt "Hero subheading (marketing prose). Keep the product/tech names verbatim: 'ng-linguo', 'Angular', 'SignalStore', 'HTML'. 'signals'/'store methods' are Angular Signals concepts; 'reads'/'writes' are data access, not literal reading/writing"
msgid "ng-linguo is a complete internationalization solution for Angular built on a SignalStore. Reads are signals, writes are store methods, and translators never see a line of HTML. Flip the language switcher above and watch every example below re-render reactively."
msgstr "ng-linguo est une solution d'internationalisation complète pour Angular, basée sur un SignalStore. Les lectures sont des signaux, les écritures sont des méthodes de store, et les traducteurs ne voient jamais une ligne de HTML. Basculez le sélecteur de langue ci-dessus et observez chaque exemple ci-dessous se re-rendre de manière réactive."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:101
msgctxt "Section heading: initial setup / installation of the library"
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "Configuration"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:108
msgctxt "Card title. 'store' = the ng-linguo SignalStore (a noun); 'Bootstrap' = set up / initialize"
msgid "Bootstrap the store"
msgstr "Amorcer le store"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:112
msgctxt "Card body (developer-docs tone). Keep API names verbatim: provideTranslate(), restoreLang(). 'store' = the SignalStore; 'loads' = fetches translations; 'Dictionaries' = the JSON translation files; 'keyed by source string' = the English text is the lookup key"
msgid "provideTranslate() wires up the store; it never loads automatically — restoreLang() is the explicit kick-off. Dictionaries are plain JSON keyed by source string."
msgstr "provideTranslate() connecte le store ; il ne se charge jamais automatiquement — restoreLang() est le déclenchement explicite. Les dictionnaires sont des fichiers JSON simples, indexés par la chaîne source."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:122
msgctxt "Section heading. 'pipe' is the Angular template-pipe concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol 't'"
msgid "The [code]t[/code] pipe"
msgstr "Le pipe [code]t[/code]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:131
msgctxt "Card title. 'template' = the Angular HTML template"
msgid "Translate in the template"
msgstr "Traduire dans le template"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:134
msgctxt "Card body. 'key' = the lookup key; 'falls through to the source' = shows the original English when no translation exists; 'blank' = empty"
msgid "The source English string is the key. With no translation it falls through to the source, so the UI is never blank."
msgstr "La chaîne source anglaise est la clé. Sans traduction, elle revient à la source, ainsi l'interface utilisateur n'est jamais vide."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:139
#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:162
msgid "He was driving incredibly fast!"
msgstr "Il conduisait incroyablement vite !"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:145
msgctxt "Section heading. 'directive' is the Angular directive concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol '[t]'"
msgid "The [code][[t][/code] directive"
msgstr "La directive [code][[t][/code]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:154
msgctxt "Card title. 'element' = an HTML / DOM element"
msgid "Translate an element"
msgstr "Traduire un élément"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:157
msgctxt "Card body. 'signals' = Angular Signals; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file; 'directive' = the Angular [t] directive; 'subscription bookkeeping' = manually managing RxJS subscriptions"
msgid "Reads through to the store's signals — once a dictionary loads, the directive re-renders with no subscription bookkeeping."
msgstr "Accède aux signaux du store — une fois qu'un dictionnaire est chargé, la directive se re-rend sans gestion manuelle des abonnements."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:173
msgctxt "Card title. 'TypeScript' is the programming language name — keep verbatim"
msgid "Translate in TypeScript"
msgstr "Traduire en TypeScript"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:176
msgctxt "Card body. 'the pipe' = the Angular t pipe; 'component code' = TypeScript class code; keep computed() verbatim; 'params' = the ICU parameters; 'reactive' = updates automatically"
msgid "The pipe's counterpart for component code. Read it inside a computed() and it stays reactive to both params and the active language."
msgstr "L'équivalent du pipe pour le code de composant. Lisez-le à l'intérieur d'un computed() et il reste réactif aux paramètres et à la langue active."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:197
msgctxt "Section heading: grammatical plural forms (one file / many files)"
msgid "Plurals"
msgstr "Pluriels"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:204
msgctxt "Card title. 'Cardinal plurals' = counting forms (1 file / 2 files), as opposed to ordinals"
msgid "Cardinal plurals across languages"
msgstr "Pluriels cardinaux dans différentes langues"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:208
msgctxt "Card body. EN/PL = English/Polish; one/few/many/other are CLDR plural-category names — keep them in English; 'count' is a variable name (keep); 'category switch' = the plural form changing"
msgid "EN has one/other; PL has one/few/many/other; an exact 0 variant reads better than '0'. Walk count through 1, 2, 5, 22 in Polish to see the category switch."
msgstr "L'anglais utilise one/other ; le polonais utilise one/few/many/other ; une variante exacte pour 0 est plus lisible que '0'. Faites varier le compteur (count) à 1, 2, 5, 22 en polonais pour observer le changement de catégorie."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:242
msgctxt "Section heading: ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …), not cardinal counts"
msgid "Ordinals"
msgstr "Ordinaux"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:249
msgctxt "Card title. 'Ordinal' = ranking forms (1st/2nd/3rd); 'categories' = the CLDR plural categories"
msgid "Ordinal categories"
msgstr "Catégories ordinales"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:253
msgctxt "Card body. st/nd/rd/th are the English ordinal suffixes; one/two/few/other are CLDR category names (keep in English); EN/PL/DE = English/Polish/German; '{n}.' shows the number followed by a period"
msgid "EN uses st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other); PL and DE collapse to a plain '{n}.'."
msgstr "L'anglais utilise st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other) ; le polonais et l'allemand se réduisent à un simple '{n}.'."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:288
msgctxt "Section heading. 'select' is the ICU MessageFormat 'select' construct (pick a variant by gender) — not a dropdown and not the verb 'to select'"
msgid "Gender select"
msgstr "Sélection par genre"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:295
msgctxt "Card title. 'Select' = the ICU select construct (choose a variant by value), not a dropdown; 'a string' = a text value"
msgid "Select on a string"
msgstr "Sélectionner sur une chaîne"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:299
msgctxt "Card body. 'pronoun' = he/she/they; 'gendered past-tense verb' = a verb form that changes with gender (as in Polish); 'count × gender' = the combination of both; 'cross-product' = every combination"
msgid "EN swaps the pronoun; PL swaps the gendered past-tense verb. The second line combines count × gender — a cross-product that differs per language."
msgstr "L'anglais change le pronom ; le polonais change le verbe au passé genré. La deuxième ligne combine le nombre × le genre — un produit croisé qui diffère selon les langues."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:322
msgctxt "Section heading: locale-aware number formatting (digit-group separators)"
msgid "Number formatting"
msgstr "Formatage des nombres"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:329
msgctxt "Card title. 'grouping' = digit-group separators in numbers (1,000 vs 1.000 vs 1 000); 'Locale-aware' = follows the active language"
msgid "Locale-aware grouping"
msgstr "Regroupement sensible à la locale"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:333
msgctxt "Card body. ':number' is an ICU formatter token (keep verbatim); en/de/pl = English/German/Polish; the figures show how each locale groups digits"
msgid "The :number formatter follows the active locale: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567."
msgstr "Le formateur :number suit la locale active : en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:344
msgctxt "Section heading. 'Context' = the translation disambiguation feature (gettext msgctxt); 'homonyms' = words spelled the same but meaning different things"
msgid "Context (homonyms)"
msgstr "Contexte (homonymes)"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:351
msgctxt "Card title about homonyms / disambiguation"
msgid "Same word, different meaning"
msgstr "Même mot, sens différent"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:354
msgctxt "Card body. 'context' is the ng-linguo option name (keep verbatim); 'key' = lookup key; 'gettext msgctxt' is a technical term (keep); 'note for translators' = a hint; 'sense' = meaning"
msgid "context is part of the key (gettext msgctxt) and doubles as a note for translators. Switch to Polish to see each sense diverge."
msgstr "context fait partie de la clé (gettext msgctxt) et sert également de note pour les traducteurs. Passez au polonais pour voir chaque sens diverger."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:361
msgctxt "audio player"
msgid "Play"
msgstr "Lecture"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:361
msgctxt "game"
msgid "Play"
msgstr "Jouer"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:364
msgctxt "direction"
msgid "Right"
msgstr "Droite"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:364
msgctxt "correct"
msgid "Right"
msgstr "Juste"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:368
msgctxt "sequence"
msgid "Order"
msgstr "Ordre"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:368
msgctxt "purchase"
msgid "Order"
msgstr "Commande"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:372
msgctxt "no cost"
msgid "Free"
msgstr "Gratuit"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:372
msgctxt "available"
msgid "Free"
msgstr "Libre"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:380
msgctxt "Section heading. 'Rich text' = text with links/emphasis; 'slot tags' = the [name] bracket placeholders ng-linguo uses in translations"
msgid "Rich text (slot tags)"
msgstr "Texte enrichi (balises de slot)"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:387
msgctxt "Card title. 'emphasis' = bold/italic styling; 'dictionary' = the JSON translation file. The point: no HTML appears in translation files"
msgid "Links and emphasis without HTML in the dictionary"
msgstr "Liens et mise en évidence sans HTML dans le dictionnaire"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:391
msgctxt "Card body. 'named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; keep 'ng-template tFor' verbatim; 'literal bracket' = a real [ character; 'XSS' is the web-security term (keep); 'zero by construction' = impossible by design. [[name] shows an escaped literal bracket — keep the doubled brackets"
msgid "Translators see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — each binds to your own ng-template tFor, with no predefined HTML. Need a literal bracket in your prose? Double the opening one. Translator content is never inserted as HTML; XSS surface is zero by construction."
msgstr "Les traducteurs voient des slots nommés comme [[name]…[[/name] — chacun se lie à votre propre ng-template tFor, sans HTML prédéfini. Besoin d'un crochet littéral dans votre texte ? Doublez le crochet ouvrant. Le contenu du traducteur n'est jamais inséré comme HTML ; la surface d'attaque XSS est nulle par construction."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:397
msgctxt "Onboarding hint. [docs] wraps a link to the documentation — translate the wrapped word too and keep the [docs] tags around it"
msgid "Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started"
msgstr "Lisez la [docs]documentation[/docs] pour commencer"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:405
msgctxt "Consent line shown before sign-up. [terms] wraps a link; 'Terms of Service' is the standard name of the legal agreement — use the conventional target-language equivalent"
msgid "By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]"
msgstr "En continuant, vous acceptez nos [terms]Conditions d'utilisation[/terms]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:413
msgctxt "Warning before a destructive, irreversible action. [warn] wraps the emphasized lead word 'Warning:'"
msgid "[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone"
msgstr "[warn]Attention :[/warn] cette action est irréversible"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:422
msgctxt "Demo of ng-linguo's slot syntax and its bracket escape. 'Escaped' is the programming sense (made literal via the [[ escape), not fleeing; 'stays literal' = shown as plain text; 'slot' = a fillable [name] region. [[b]bold[[/b] is escaped literal text, [b]this[/b] is a real slot — keep both forms exactly"
msgid "Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot"
msgstr "[[b]bold[[/b] échappé reste littéral — [b]ceci[/b] est un slot"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:433
msgctxt "Consent line with a nested slot. [link] wraps a link to the Terms; [b] emphasizes a word inside it. 'Terms and Conditions' is the standard legal-document name — use the conventional target-language equivalent"
msgid "Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]"
msgstr "Acceptez nos [link]Conditions [b]Générales[/b][/link]"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:450
msgctxt "Section heading. 'ESLint' is a tool name — keep verbatim; 'a11y' is the numeronym for accessibility (keep, or use the target word for accessibility)"
msgid "ESLint & a11y"
msgstr "ESLint et a11y"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:457
msgctxt "Card title (colloquial). 'linter' = ESLint; 'keep the linter happy' = satisfy the lint rule; '[t]' is a code symbol (keep); 'empty elements' = elements with no text content"
msgid "Keep the linter happy with empty [t] elements"
msgstr "Contenter le linter avec des éléments [t] vides"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:461
msgctxt "Card body. Keep verbatim: @angular-eslint/template/elements-content, [t]. 'a11y' = accessibility; 'markup' = HTML; 'fallback' = the default shown before translations load; 'the hero' = the large heading at the top of the page"
msgid "The a11y rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content flags empty headings, anchors, and buttons. A [t] element fills its text at runtime, so the source string can move out of the markup entirely — the headings on this page are empty [t] elements; only the hero keeps its text as a fallback."
msgstr "La règle d'accessibilité @angular-eslint/template/elements-content signale les titres, ancres et boutons vides. Un élément [t] remplit son texte à l'exécution, ainsi la chaîne source peut être entièrement retirée du balisage — les titres de cette page sont des éléments [t] vides ; seul le titre principal conserve son texte comme solution de repli."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:471
msgctxt "Section heading: translating the app automatically using an AI / LLM"
msgid "Translating with AI"
msgstr "Traduction avec l'IA"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:478
msgctxt "Card title. 'source string' = the original English text; 'catalog' = the translation file (.po)"
msgid "From source string to translated catalog"
msgstr "De la chaîne source au catalogue traduit"

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:482
msgctxt "Card body. Keep verbatim: extract CLI, gettext, .po, JSON, ng-linguo, SDK, API key, translator. 'catalogs' = translation files; 'chat model' = an LLM; 'merges the reply' = applies the response; 'clipboard copy/paste' = manual copying"
msgid "The extract CLI keeps gettext .po catalogs and compiles them to runtime JSON. Translate by copying a prompt into any chat model, or fully automatically: point translator at a module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, you keep the SDK and the API key. Omit translator and translation stays a clipboard copy/paste."
msgstr "L'interface de ligne de commande (CLI) extract gère les catalogues gettext .po et les compile en JSON pour l'exécution. Traduisez en copiant une invite dans n'importe quel modèle de chat, ou de manière entièrement automatique : dirigez translator vers un module qui appelle votre propre fournisseur d'IA — ng-linguo écrit l'invite et fusionne la réponse, vous conservez le SDK et la clé API. Omettez translator et la traduction reste un copier-coller manuel."

#: apps/playground/src/app/app.html:491
msgctxt "Page footer. 'ng-linguo' is the product name (keep verbatim); 'living documentation' = documentation that is also a working demo"
msgid "Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation."
msgstr "Construit avec ng-linguo · ce bac à sable est aussi une documentation vivante."

